cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: ovito-auto-viz
abstract: >-
  Declarative, reproducible OVITO visualization of LAMMPS files: YAML
  viz-cards rendered to publication-quality images, comparison grids,
  movies, or ready-to-open OVITO sessions, with all crystallographic
  labels (Burgers vectors, line directions, character angles) computed
  from the data itself and full provenance embedded in every output.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bitzek
    given-names: Erik
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7430-3694"
    email: e.bitzek@mpi-susmat.de
    affiliation: >-
      Max-Planck-Institut for Sustainable Materials, Düsseldorf, Germany;
      Institute of Materials Simulation (WW8), Friedrich-Alexander-Universität
      Erlangen-Nürnberg (FAU), Fürth, Germany
repository-code: "https://github.com/biterik/ovito-auto-viz"
url: "https://github.com/biterik/ovito-auto-viz"
license: BSD-3-Clause
version: 0.3.0
date-released: 2026-08-04
keywords:
  - OVITO
  - LAMMPS
  - molecular dynamics
  - dislocations
  - visualization
  - materials science
  - reproducibility
